Feature: GPU flag "guest_refresh_hz" (the guest's vblank rate, for frame rates above 60)

Applies to: rexglue-sdk nightly-20260921-923c1a59 (thirdparty/rexglue-sdk)
Apply with: git -C thirdparty/rexglue-sdk apply ../../patches/rexglue-sdk/0010-guest-refresh-rate.patch
Status:     local patch (a feature for our port, not a bug fix)

WHY
  A game that presents with vsync (D3D interval 1, or Crash's PDDI "one
  vblank per frame" mode) waits for the next guest vblank every frame. The
  SDK fires vblanks at the video mode's refresh rate (video_mode_refresh_rate,
  60 Hz), so such a game can never pass 60 fps, however fast the host.

WHAT
  A hot-reloadable int flag guest_refresh_hz (default 0 = the video mode's
  rate, range 0-1000). The vblank thread reads it on every iteration, so it
  can change while running. Only the vblank rate changes: the video mode the
  game queries still reports 60 Hz.

HOW WE FOUND / CHECKED IT (2026-09-30)
  Crash: Mind over Mutant with --fps_cap=144 (our frame_rate.cpp sets this
  flag to the cap, and lifts the game's own 1/60 s minimum frame step with a
  midasm hook): 142 fps in gameplay. Same run with --guest_refresh_hz=60 given
  explicitly: 60.0 fps. Both limits have to go.

diff --git a/src/graphics/graphics_system.cpp b/src/graphics/graphics_system.cpp
index 8f2fcb0..88d4d43 100644
--- a/src/graphics/graphics_system.cpp
+++ b/src/graphics/graphics_system.cpp
@@ -35,6 +35,17 @@ REXCVAR_DEFINE_STRING(swap_post_effect, "none", "GPU", "Swap post effect: none,
     .allowed({"none", "fxaa", "fxaa_extreme"})
     .lifecycle(rex::cvar::Lifecycle::kRequiresRestart);
 
+// Mind over Recomp: the guest's vblank rate. The game's frames wait for the
+// next vblank (D3D's flip queue, PDDI's swap), so the 60 Hz of the NTSC video
+// mode capped it at 60 fps however fast the host is. A higher rate here lets
+// such a game present more often; the host's own display rate is separate
+// (the presenter). Read every iteration of the vblank thread, so it can
+// change while running.
+REXCVAR_DEFINE_INT32(guest_refresh_hz, 0, "GPU",
+                     "Guest vblank rate in Hz (0 = the video mode's, 60 for NTSC). Higher lets "
+                     "games that wait for vblank run faster")
+    .range(0, 1000)
+    .lifecycle(rex::cvar::Lifecycle::kHotReload);
 REXCVAR_DEFINE_BOOL(store_shaders, true, "GPU",
                     "Store shaders persistently and load them when loading games to avoid "
                     "runtime spikes and freezes when playing the game not for the first time.");
@@ -152,14 +163,17 @@ X_STATUS GraphicsSystem::SetupGuestGpu(runtime::FunctionDispatcher* function_dis
